  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Surgical and Medical Instrument Manufacturing (NAICS 339112) has received $118M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The market has 681 awards so far, with an average award size of $173K. Obligations fell 89.3% year over year. Fiscal-year comparisons show a decline from earlier peaks: FY22 obligations were $1.1B, FY23 obligations were $1.6B, FY24 obligations were $2B, FY25 obligations were $1.6B, and FY26 obligations were $1.1B. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the dominant buyer in FY2027 to date, obligating $115M. The Department of Justice is the next-largest buyer with $2.2M in obligations. The Department of State, Department of Health and Human Services, and Environmental Protection Agency recorded $52.1K, $48.1K, and $35.6K respectively. WELCH ALLYN, INC. leads vendors with $31.6M in obligations. OLYMPUS AMERICA INC follows with $22.8M. Other notable vendors include SDV OFFICE SYSTEMS LLC with $8.9M and SCRIPTPRO USA INC with $7.8M. All current-year totals are partial because FY2027 is fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated is buying in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer, obligating $115M in FY2027 to date. The next-largest buyer is the Department of Justice with $2.2M. Several agencies recorded only thousands or zero in obligations, for example the Department of State at $52.1K and the Department of the Interior at $0. This shows buying is heavily concentrated in one agency in the current fiscal year to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who captured the most contract dollars in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "WELCH ALLYN, INC. captured the most obligations with $31.6M. OLYMPUS AMERICA INC captured $22.8M, followed by SDV OFFICE SYSTEMS LLC with $8.9M and SCRIPTPRO USA INC with $7.8M. A group of vendors together account for the majority of the FY2027 to date obligations listed among the top vendors."
      }
    ]
  },
